+===== arc progress --help =====
+Where each series of work stands: its items, their stages, and what waits on a person. Read on request; nothing else prints it.
+
+A series is a `progress` journal artifact whose items are journal events, one per edit. A linked item's stage is what its change's events in the ledger holding it record, this project's or another registered project's; `arc status` is the live reading. Without an argument, every series not retired, each in full, then each related series of another project in compact form. The default is a view for a person, painted when standard output is a terminal; `--plain` prints every recorded fact as text and `--json` the versioned `arc-progress/1`. See `arc guide progress`.
+
+Usage: arc progress [OPTIONS] [SERIES]
+       arc progress <COMMAND>
+
+Commands:
+  start     Start a series: write a `progress` artifact and declare its items
+  add       Add an item, at the end unless placed; prints its id
+  rename    Rename an item; its id stays
+  move      Move an item before or after another
+  drop      Drop an item with a reason; it stays visible and leaves the count
+  done      Mark done an item no change carries
+  reopen    Reopen a done or dropped item, linked or not
+  link      Link an item to a change, of this project's ledger or another's
+  unlink    Remove an item's link to its change
+  source    Bind an item to its originating journal artifact (`todo`, `feature-request`, `plan`, or `handoff`)
+  unsource  Remove an item's originating journal artifact link
+  waves     Manage declared waves on a series (add, rename, move, remove)
+  wave      Assign a standing item to a declared wave
+  unwave    Remove an item's wave assignment
+  depend    Record an explicit prerequisite on a standing item (refuses cycles)
+  undepend  Remove a recorded prerequisite from an item
+  wait      Say an item waits on a question of this journal
+  unwait    Remove the question an item was said to wait on
+  split     Split an item into several; the original shows as split and leaves the count
+  transfer  Transfer or defer an item to another progress series (local or cross-project) [alias: defer]
+  relate    Relate a series to a series in another project
+  unrelate  Remove a relation this project's series records
+  retire    Retire a series as superseded by its conclusion
+  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
+
+Arguments:
+  [SERIES]
+          A series, by filename or topic. Omitted, every series of this project that is not retired
+
