+===== arc journal reopen --help =====
+Reverse a recorded consumption without rewriting the event log.
+
+Appends typed `reopened` events under the event lock bound (`reopens`) to each active unreversed consumption selected under the transition lock, so each named artifact returns to the state it held before the consumption without clearing a distinct, later consumption during replica exchange; history keeps both `consumed` and `reopened` events. Structural handoff consumptions (`journal transition`, `begin --from-journal`, and `journal promote --global`) are protected in both selectors. Explicit filenames bind a reversal to every active unreversed consumption on each named artifact; the `--session` / `--since` (and optional `--until`) batch form selects only currently consumed non-handoff artifacts whose standing (and every active) consumption belongs to that session and window, skipping artifacts carrying another active consumption outside the window. `--dry-run` names each matched artifact without writing anything. `--global` targets the operator journal.
+
+Usage: arc journal reopen [OPTIONS] --reason <REASON> [FILES]...
+
+Arguments:
+  [FILES]...
+          Artifact filenames inside the journal dir (names, not paths). Required unless reopening by `--session` and `--since`
+
+Options:
+      --actor <ACTOR>
+          Acting identity; see `arc guide identity-options`
+
+      --global
+          Target the operator journal at <ai-home>/arc/journals/global, from any directory. All journal kinds share this scope. With promote, the source is a project memory and the destination is global
+
+      --session <ID>
+          Reopen every currently consumed artifact whose standing (and every active) consumption was recorded by this session inside the `--since`/`--until` window. Pass an explicit acting session before `reopen` (or via `ARC_SESSION`)
+
+      --harness <HARNESS>
+          Acting harness; see `arc guide identity-options`
+          
+          [env: ARC_HARNESS]
+
+      --since <TIME>
+          Inclusive start of the consumption window: RFC 3339 or journal stamp (`YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ`), used with `--session`
+
+      --until <TIME>
+          Inclusive end of the consumption window: RFC 3339 or journal stamp (`YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ`), used with `--session` and `--since`
+
+      --reason <REASON>
+          Why the consumption is reversed, recorded on each `reopened` event
+
+      --session-link <SESSION_LINK>
+          Private acting-session link; see `arc guide identity-options`
